  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;STEPHEN M. O'MARA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stephen M. O'Mara was an Irish businessman and republican politician in Limerick, born on 5 January 1884 and died on 11 November 1959. He was the third son of Stephen O'Mara, Snr, a former Mayor of Limerick and briefly an Irish Parliamentary Party MP. He married Nancy O'Brien and had a son named Peter. His elder brother James was an early supporter of Sinn Féin, which Stephen also joined after the Easter Rising. He was a member of Limerick Corporation during the Irish War of Independence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Stephen M. O'Mara was an Irish businessman and republican politician in Limerick, born on 5 January 1884 and died on 11 November 1959. He was the third son of Stephen O'Mara, Snr, a former Mayor of Limerick and briefly an Irish Parliamentary Party MP. He married Nancy O'Brien and had a son named Peter. His elder brother James was an early supporter of Sinn Féin, which influenced Stephen's political views. He was a member of Limerick Corporation during the Irish War of Independence."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STEPHEN O'MARA, SNR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stephen O'Mara, Snr was a former Mayor of Limerick and briefly an Irish Parliamentary Party MP."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NANCY O'BRIEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nancy O'Brien was the wife of Stephen M. O'Mara and mother of his son, Peter."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PETER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Peter is the son of Stephen M. O'Mara and Nancy O'Brien."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAMES O'MARA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"James O'Mara was the elder brother of Stephen M. O'Mara and an early supporter of Sinn Féin, which influenced Stephen's political views."&lt;SEP&gt;"James O'Mara was the father of Stephen O'Mara (senator) and an early supporter of Isaac Butt, owning a bacon factory in Limerick."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SINN FÉIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sinn Féin is a political party in Ireland, supported by James O'Mara and later by Stephen M. O'Mara."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GEORGE CLANCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"George Clancy was the Mayor of Limerick who was killed by the Black and Tans during the Irish War of Independence."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLACK AND TANS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Black and Tans were paramilitary police in Ireland during the Irish War of Independence, responsible for the killing of Mayor George Clancy."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STEPHEN O'MARA (SENATOR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stephen O'Mara (senator) was an Irish nationalist politician and businessman from Limerick, born on 26 December 1844 and died on 26 July 1926. His father, James O'Mara, was an early supporter of Isaac Butt and owned a bacon factory in Limerick. Stephen married Ellen Pigott in 1867 and had 12 children, of whom the first three died of diphtheria in 1872. His sons, James and Stephen, Jnr, became prominent Irish republicans and radicalized their father's political views. He joined Limerick Corporation around 1880, becoming the first Nationalist Mayor."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOSEPH O'MARA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Joseph O'Mara was the brother of Stephen O'Mara (senator) and became an opera singer."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELLEN PIGOTT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ellen Pigott was the wife of Stephen O'Mara (senator) and mother of his 12 children."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTERBORO HIGH SCHOOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Interboro High School is the high school attended by the individual mentioned in Document 3."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEST CHESTER UNIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"West Chester University is the institution where the individual mentioned in Document 3 earned her Bachelor of Arts degree in history and a certificate in Secondary Education."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF PENNSYLVANIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"University of Pennsylvania is the institution where the individual mentioned in Document 3 received her Master's degree in liberal studies."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PENNSYLVANIA HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pennsylvania House of Representatives is the legislative body where the individual mentioned in Document 3 served."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIMERICK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Limerick is a city in Ireland where both Stephen M. O'Mara and Stephen O'Mara (senator) were from and had significant roles."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISAAC BUTT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Isaac Butt was a political figure whose support influenced James O'Mara's political views."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACON FACTORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacon Factory was owned by James O'Mara and operated in Limerick."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IRISH WAR OF INDEPENDENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Irish War of Independence was a period during which Stephen M. O'Mara and Stephen O'Mara (senator) were involved in politics."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;STEPHEN M. O'MARA&quot;" target="&quot;JAMES O'MARA&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"James O'Mara was the elder brother of Stephen M. O'Mara and influenced his political views through his support of Sinn Féin."</data>
      <data key="d5">"brotherhood, political influence"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0121-1fbb6efea06e</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
